text:
To sum it up... [may contain spoilers]
Bad points:
- The game was shorter than expected;
- The fights were simpler than expected;
- The phase mechanics were way too linear (see a manhole in the beginning of a train station? You know you're coming back from there. No multi-paths or multiple options of choice that impact story despite maybe the bus stuff, etc).
Good points:
- Awesome art;
- Good music/sound fx;
- Awesome story (but should be more exploited);
- Good mechanics (some people are ranting about this one, but I think some "issues" with the playability are made exactly to put the gamer to work... you don't see people complaining about Mario jumps being "too low" in Super Mario. So you shouldn't be complaining about this game's playability either)
Overall it was a very good story, but sadly it was also too short. There should be more talks, more stops, more explanation, etc (being it with another character after main's death or not). I just think this game had way too much potential that could be easily used to make a 20-50h gameplay instead of 4-5h.
Anyway, good game, looking forward to play a sequel (or prequel about the first alien contact, or even a spin-off from another character's POV... who knows).
If you have some money in your pocket without use, give it a try.

